pagerbot: :rotating_light: [INCIDENT P0] Elevated 5xx and high tail latency on /v1/generate (us-east-1) starting ~2026-03-15T02:14Z. Error rate ~12% (baseline ~0.2%). Paging @anya_oncall and @mike_sre. Details: https://pager/redwood/incidents/INC-4721

anya_oncall: I'm oncall-ack. Quick triage: traffic concentrated to tokens tk-A and tk-B, heavy streaming and very long contexts (many >8k). KV cache miss rate spiked, and we see long running GPU queue depth. Possible client-side fanout + lack of idempotency causing retries.

mike_sre: taking pager. Initial plan for live mitigation: 1) soft per-token concurrency cap 2) temporary per-token quota reduction (throttle new requests) 3) disable streaming for the offending tokens 4) edge-level rate limiting for the CIDR group. Ops please apply caps while I coordinate measurements.

ops-runner: applying per-token concurrency cap=8 for tokens tk-A,tk-B now. Command run: `rctl apply --scope token --tokens tk-A,tk-B --concurrency 8` -> OK. Pushing edge rule: `edgectl rate-limit create --match token:tk-A --rps 5 --burst 10 --duration 600s` -> OK.

anya_oncall: after caps + edge rule we're seeing 5xx drop from 12% -> 4.1% in the last 3m, p95 tail latency improving. Customers still degrade for long streaming clients.

jen_support: sending targeted notice to affected customers (acct-A, acct-B). Draft: "We're applying temporary throttles to reduce service instability; please apply client-side backoff and idempotency as recommended. We'll follow up with mitigation timeline." Want to sync wording with legal/pm? :eyes:

kevin_sdk: Preparing the SDK advisory now. Short actionable guidance to include in the support note and customers' engineering channels: recommended retry policy (non-streaming), idempotency header, and a temporary streaming fallback. Posting snippet below that you can paste in the notices.

kevin_sdk: SDK retry example (JS):
```
// Recommended transient failure retry
const retryPolicy = {
  initialDelayMs: 200,
  multiplier: 2,
  maxDelayMs: 10000,
  maxAttempts: 6,
  jitter: true // full jitter recommended
};

async function callWithRetries(fn) {
  let attempt = 0;
  let delay = retryPolicy.initialDelayMs;
  while (attempt < retryPolicy.maxAttempts) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      if (!isTransient(err) || attempt === retryPolicy.maxAttempts - 1) throw err;
      await sleep(randomJitter(delay));
      delay = Math.min(retryPolicy.maxDelayMs, delay * retryPolicy.multiplier);
      attempt++;
    }
  }
}

// Idempotency: include a stable UUID per logical request
const headers = { 'Idempotency-Key': generateUuid() };
```

kevin_sdk: Curl example for idempotent call / disabling streaming quickly:
```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate
  -H "Authorization: Bearer tk-A"
  -H "Idempotency-Key: $(uuidgen)"
  -H "X-Redwood-Streaming: disable"
  -d '{"input":"..."}'
```

kevin_sdk: Quick guidance to customers to mitigate impact client-side: 
- Switch off streaming (or fall back to polling) for the next 30–60m.
- Use idempotency keys for retryable operations.
- Implement exponential backoff with full jitter (see snippet).
- Reduce parallel/concurrent requests (client-side concurrency cap ~4).

mike_sre: Confirming metrics after second mitigation wave: error-rate down to 1.8% and queue depth normalized. p99 latencies still trending high for one actor (acct-B).

ops-runner: Applied temporary quota reduction to acct-B: 50% of baseline, will auto-lift in 30m unless we see stability. Command used: `quotactl adjust --account acct-B --pct 50 --ttl 1800s` -> OK.

sre_lead: Nice quick work. Follow-ups for postmortem/action items: 1) add runtime auto-detect for token-fingerprint fanout and auto-soft-throttle (nonblocking) 2) surface per-token streaming concurrency in console 3) add automated customer advisory template in support playbook 4) update SDK docs with the retry/idempotency snippet and recommended values.

anya_oncall: Only remaining task: confirm with support that affected customers received the advisory and didn't hit escalations. Jen, update when done.

jen_support: Sent messages to primary contacts for acct-A and acct-B. acct-A replied: "Thanks, adjusting client concurrency. Will revert streaming." acct-B asked for ETA on quota lift; answered ~30m, monitoring.

mike_sre: marking incident as mitigated for live traffic. We'll keep post-incident review. If anyone wants to dig into logs: run `logq query --from now-1h --filter "token:tk-B OR token:tk-A" --fields status,latency,streaming`

kevin_sdk: I'll open an SDK PR to add a short "operational guidance" page with code samples and a small troubleshooting checklist (toggle streaming, idempotency, backoff parameters).

pagerbot: :white_check_mark: Incident INC-4721 transitioned to MITIGATED at 2026-03-15T02:42Z. Follow-up: create INC-4721-POSTMORTEM and link to SDK/docs PR.

mike_sre: +1 to automated detection. Also suggest we add a short circuit-breaker recommendation for clients: if you see >10% 5xx across 1m window, reduce concurrency by 50% and apply backoff. We'll capture exact numbers in postmortem.

sre_lead: Agreed. I'll own the postmortem. Assigning tasks in the ticket: add timeline, root cause (client fanout + missing idempotency + long contexts), mitigations performed, and action items for SDK/docs/console.

